#! ia 1.0

@capability workspace-method
  meaning
    says "Work with workspace records under the IA methodology: the workspace-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a workspace. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a workspace?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook workspace-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook workspace-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with workspace records, each an explicit work boundary grouping systems, whose sources name the roots its records are captured from: orient through ia position --word workspace and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with workspace records?"
  subject
    subject-word workspace
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word workspace at the seat the work concerns, read the workspace records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary workspace --schema for the sections and fields a workspace carries."
      Inference means "Run ia position with no seat for the workspace's systems, sources, steward and mandates."
      Decision means "workspace is a word of workspace-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/workspace-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these workspace records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the workspace must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Decide whether the work fits the systems the workspace composes, or needs one installed first."
      Decision means "Extend an existing workspace through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the workspace will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the workspace; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Change the existing workspace's composition through --set, for example to add an installed system; a repository with no workspace needs ia init, which is the person's call."
      Decision means "Change the workspace record only through ia preview --set, then ia author with the digest it returned, then ia validate; designing new workspaces lies outside this kit (by hand from the public IA documentation, or with an InventArch subscription)."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Run ia validate over the whole workspace, and ia position again to see that the seats still resolve."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the workspace, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability distribution-method
  meaning
    says "Work with distribution records under the IA methodology: the distribution-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a distribution. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a distribution?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook distribution-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook distribution-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with distribution records, each the root records from which a distributable closure is selected: orient through ia position --word distribution and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with distribution records?"
  subject
    subject-word distribution
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word distribution at the seat the work concerns, read the distribution records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary distribution --schema for the sections and fields a distribution carries."
      Inference means "Read the distributions the workspace pins in .ia/distributions.lock.json and the root records each ships."
      Decision means "distribution is a word of workspace-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/workspace-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these distribution records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the distribution must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Decide which kit or distribution the work needs, and the version the workspace should pin."
      Decision means "Extend an existing distribution through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the distribution will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the distribution; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Install with ia install <id>@<version> --catalog <catalog> --apply --yes, or reinstall the locked generation with ia restore --apply --yes, asking the person first: both write files they commit."
      Decision means "Install, restore and read distributions; authoring a new distribution or kit lies outside this kit (by hand from the public IA documentation, or with an InventArch subscription)."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Run ia validate after the install, and report what the lock now pins."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the distribution, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."
